AB  - The article presents mSEC-AT, an AI-driven tool designed to automate security audits of Android applications within DevSecOps environments. By integrating tools such as CodeQL, Trivy, and MobSF, the system collects technical evidence that is automatically mapped by a Large Language Model against a catalog of 469 security requirements. This approach enables semantic compliance assessment, producing narrative and fully traceable reports. Validated using the OpenMRS application, the tool demonstrated its efficiency by conducting comprehensive analyses in a matter of minutes, thereby enhancing vulnerability detection and supporting informed decision-making.
